## Approach

- Start from the end of both arrays.
- Use three pointers to keep track of the elements in `nums1`, `nums2`, and the position where the next element should go.
- Compare the elements from both arrays.
- Put the larger element at the end of `nums1`.
- Continue until all elements from `nums2` are added.
- Merging from the back avoids overwriting the elements already present in `nums1`.
